server: allow the NLS directory to be set by environment.

wineserver dies on Android with

    wineserver: failed to load l_intl.nls

while l_intl.nls is sitting in the package at share/wine/nls/. All four places
it looks are unreachable here:

  - get_nls_dir() derives the path from realpath("/proc/self/exe"). The app
    cannot execve a file in its own data directory, so wineserver is started as
    an argument to /system/bin/linker64 and /proc/self/exe is the linker -- the
    search lands under /apex/com.android.runtime.
  - The remaining three are absolute paths under /usr, on a read-only system
    partition where nothing can be installed.

It is a fatal_error, not a warning, so the case mapping table is simply absent.

Adding WINENLSDIR ahead of the existing entries is the same shape as the
WINEDLLPATH fallback that tools/wine/wine.c already has for the identical
reason, and it changes nothing when the variable is unset.

Note that ntdll needs no equivalent: it finds its own NLS data through dladdr()
on ntdll.so, which stays correct under the linker. Only wineserver, a separate
executable, asks the kernel who it is.

Not suitable upstream as-is: upstream would want this driven by configure or by
a general datadir override rather than a single-purpose variable.

--- a/server/unicode.c
+++ b/server/unicode.c
